# serializer version: 1
# name: test_a_destroy_plan_runs_from_the_bottom_up
  '''
  <!-- lely:destroy:dev -->
  ### lely destroy plan · target `dev`
  
  `https://dbc-example.cloud.databricks.com` as `jane@example.com`
  
  **1 change · 0 runs · 1 destructive**
  
  ```diff
    warm  command
        skipped: not for target `dev`
    backfill  bundle.run
        skipped: `bundle.run` has nothing to destroy
    notify  command
        skipped: it needs app.resources.jobs.bar.id, which isn't there
    app  bundle
        model_version = 14  ← model.version
  -     delete   jobs.backfill  destructive
            backfill · id 771
        the bundle's uploaded files go with them
        and whatever else `bundle destroy` removes
        as seen by jane@example.com under /Workspace/Users/jane@example.com/.bundle/shop/dev
    model  ./ops/steps.py:LatestModel
        skipped: `./ops/steps.py:LatestModel` has nothing to destroy
  ```
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_a_destructive_change_is_named_above_the_plan
  '''
  <!-- lely:plan:dev:team-a -->
  ### lely plan · project `team-a` · target `dev`
  
  `https://dbc-example.cloud.databricks.com` as `jane@example.com`
  
  **2 changes · 2 runs · 1 destructive · 1 waiting**
  
  **Destructive:** `app: pipelines.foo`
  
  ```diff
    model  ./ops/steps.py:LatestModel
        → version = 14
    app  bundle
        model_version = 14  ← model.version
  +     create   jobs.bar
  -     replace  pipelines.foo  destructive
            replaced: storage (immutable)
        run      uploads the bundle's files
    notify  command
        waiting for app.resources.jobs.bar.id
    backfill  bundle.run
        bundle  ← app
        run      runs jobs.backfill
    warm  command
        skipped: not for target `dev`
  ```
  
  > Applied from a file, this stops before `notify`: a waiting step is planned once what it waits for exists.
  
  > Planned with uncommitted changes: lely can't say what this was made on, so it won't run it from a file. Commit first, or run it without one.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_a_first_deploy
